# Deliberately almost empty, and that is the point.
#
# With no .npmignore, npm falls back to .gitignore when deciding what a tarball
# carries — and this app's .gitignore lists `dist/`, which is exactly the thing
# the package exists to ship. The first publish of @fnndsc/argus went out with
# two files and no bundle because of it. `files: ["dist"]` in package.json says
# what goes in; this file stops .gitignore from taking anything back out.
node_modules/
